WEBVTT

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:05.100
Some changes are being made with the mission.

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:10.840
Am I being... removed?

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:14.890
If anything, it's the opposite.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.750
The Halcyon has reached the point of being useable.

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:19.310
The Halcyon?

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.650
It's what they built at the Akapusu...

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.330
It's the same type of craft as the Infinity.

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:26.510
We're going to have you participate with the Halcyon.

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:28.740
The Halcyon...

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars, Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて 飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Carry the unexpierence of the heart in the hands and go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて go far away

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
Urayamu koto ni Narete shimattara

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
If you have experienced the envy

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
羨む事に 慣れてしまったら

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Hokoreru jibun ga Toozakatteku

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Your proud self will go far away

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
誇れる自分が 遠ざかってく

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Mienai tsubasa de habataku no fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Flapping the invisible wings to fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
見えない翼で羽ばたくの fly higher

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
Yume wo egaku no wa hito ni umareta kara

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
I'm imaging dreams because I was born a "person"

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
夢を描くのは「人」に生まれたから

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Carry the unexperienced of the heart in the hands

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
Anata to nara Yowai jibun wo sarakedashite hashiridaseru no

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
If I were with you, I'd start running, exposing my weak self

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
あなたとなら 弱い自分をさらけ出して走り出せるの

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
Mirai yo dou ka Mugen ni tsuzuke go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
The future! Somehow continues to the infinity, go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
未来よどうか 無限に続け go far away

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:06.680
At this point, the mission's chance of success is 30%.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:06.980
Episode Twenty-Three: 
That's Why You're There 

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:11.250
Every hour, this number rises.

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:17.150
Our intelligence and our courage are opening up possibilities.

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:21.220
I'm sorry that I can't go and see you off.

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:22.000
It's okay.

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:24.350
I'll be evacuating with Arisa and the others...

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:26.890
...and right now, the mission has the top priority.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.060
Yes, you're right.

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:37.300
The Halcyon has been improving rapidly. 

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:37.270
It's only the color that's different?

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:40.800
Once finished, it will be able to process information... 

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:39.880
The shape of the head is different, too.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:42.480
...on a level that will rival that of the Foundations.

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:42.220
So big sister is going to be piloting that, right?

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:45.540
And by combining it with the Infinity's firing control systems...

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:47.890
...it will make a practical strategy possible...

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:49.360
Oh, it's an e-mail.

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:54.250
The laser cannon's adjustments are proceeding as scheduled.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.620
The deficiencies in the pressure seals' strength are cleared.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:58.940
The control programs for the accelerators...

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:00.270
...will take a little more time.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:00.810
Hmm?

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:02.200
No need to worry.

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:03.590
What about the Halcyon?

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:07.290
It looks like they're having problems integrating the systems.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:11.800
With a single pilot processing such a large amount of data, it's quite...

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:14.750
Of course, it's scheduled to be ready for the mission.

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:18.510
The evacuation of the civilians on each Foundation is complete.

00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:21.090
The evacuation of all passengers, except for the mission crew...

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:22.870
...will be finished within 24 hours.

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:25.940
As scheduled, the Akapusu, the Stellvia, the Odyssey...

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:30.420
...and the El Santo will begin heading for Pluto tomorrow.

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:39.620
Shipon.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.380
It's almost time... Shipon...

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:49.920
That woke me up!

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:52.050
Hey, aren't you a little too tired?

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:55.230
There's still more than a week until the big day, after all...

00:03:55.430 --> 00:03:57.460
...so how about getting a day or so off?

00:03:57.700 --> 00:03:58.620
I can't.

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:01.070
After all, I'm the one who's furthest behind...

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:10.410
I'm sorry!

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:14.840
It's all right. It's still not time yet.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:16.710
Right. I'm sorry.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:35.720
It feels like it's almost time...

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.260
There's only one more Fujiyama flight going to Earth.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.690
The evacuation will end there...

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:43.640
And then it's the beginning for us...

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:48.290
All right then. Let's do the final check.

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:04.100
Let's hit the showers.

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:06.370
Oh, um, I'll go later...

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:09.000
Oh... okay, then we're going ahead.

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:25.110
Everyone's rapidly becoming able to do it...

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:27.010
I'm the only one that's behind...

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:29.890
I remember around the time you entered school...

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:30.600
What?

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:33.290
No matter what you did, it got all messed up...

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.090
The only thing you were exceptional at was programming.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.670
Try believing in yourself a little more.

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:05.410
I'm sorry...

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:06.250
What?

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:07.670
The information processing...

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:10.230
...is too slow, isn't it?

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:23.050
There's still time.

00:06:23.570 --> 00:06:25.310
Look, if you just follow through...

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:29.070
...just like before, when you analyzed the aliens' message...

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:30.310
That's no good.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:34.740
I have to... I have to become better able to handle my duties.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:37.400
I'm telling you, it'll be all right if we work together.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:42.170
It won't be us working together. It'll be you rescuing me.

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:43.150
It won't be.

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:44.020
It will.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:48.160
You're a genius, Kouta, but I'm not. That's why!

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:49.190
Shima-chan!

00:06:55.730 --> 00:06:56.400
Thank you!

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:05.280
Can we be persuaded by answers as vague as...

00:07:05.350 --> 00:07:06.630
..."an open tear in space?!"

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:10.040
I'm sorry, but I have to say that the answers...

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:11.950
The Office of Space Development's answers are not enough!

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:18.450
Government Complaint Assembly

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:19.960
Government Complaint Assembly 

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:21.470
Some people are looting and such...

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:20.210
Government Complaint Assembly 

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:24.440
...but generally speaking, the disorder is within predicted levels.

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:28.000
The Foundations are the safest places, right?!

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:29.590
Let us onboard, too!

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.240
There is nothing that will influence the livelihood of the citizenry.

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:34.100
And the local governments and the police are working hard for us.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:37.450
Let's continue to emphasize that conditions...

00:07:37.520 --> 00:07:39.020
...are the same as during the Great Mission.

00:07:39.630 --> 00:07:43.040
The only solution is to hold out and defend ourselves to the end.

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:45.060
There's no place to run to.

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:47.660
Continue to make official announcements...

00:07:47.950 --> 00:07:50.500
...in regards to the mission as much as we possibly can.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:53.160
After all, in order to relieve their worries...

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:56.280
...we have to be honest with them.

00:07:56.920 --> 00:08:01.140
The Cosmic Fracture! The tear in space... space...

00:08:02.010 --> 00:08:06.030
Am I the only one who thinks that's a convenient excuse?

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:10.130
If they have a genuine understanding of the situation, then that's fine.

00:08:10.910 --> 00:08:14.820
But as long as I hear that answer, I don't believe they do.

00:08:15.310 --> 00:08:17.360
What are they doing up in space?!

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:21.690
They haven't even given us the ability to see that.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:24.390
Yet all they ask is that we cooperate.

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:26.030
So unreasonable...

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:27.360
Sir!

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:31.200
Apologize!

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:34.080
Apologize! 
Shut up!

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:36.650
If you have something to say, look people in the eye and say it!

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:37.780
Who cares?!

00:08:40.210 --> 00:08:40.840
Let go!

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:42.200
Come with us for a bit.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:45.890
Stop, let me go! Damn it, let go!

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:52.580
Thank you!

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:57.300
I admire your sense of justice.

00:08:57.900 --> 00:08:59.180
But it's sad that the young people are like that...

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:02.150
...when they're going to carry the burden of the next generation.

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:03.800
And what about you?

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:04.610
Huh?

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:07.330
I know that there are different opinions...

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:10.660
...but right now, how about thinking about what you can do?

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:14.590
All you do is stare blankly and slow things down.

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:17.480
The boy who threw that bottle, and you...

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:18.000
Sir!

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:19.450
I will fight!

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:27.740
I guess I'm not much different from him.

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:30.660
Could I have a moment of your time?

00:09:58.630 --> 00:10:00.360
Everyone's working desperately, especially Shipon.

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:02.470
Yeah, I know.

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:05.460
But Shipon's being standoffish.

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:08.840
It must be tough, dealing with both the mission and a romance.

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:10.600
I'm not mixing the mission up with romance!

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:16.240
Shima-chan is taking responsibility for every single thing herself.

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:19.010
At this rate, I don't know what to do.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:21.140
How about saying that to Shipon?

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:21.820
Eh?

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:24.800
You've never actually told her how you feel, right?

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:28.040
Why do you like Shipon, Kouta?

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:29.600
Why?

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:31.850
Yes. Why?

00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:36.420
That's right. Why in the world did you fall in love with Shipon?

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:38.300
Why?

00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:44.170
So why did you run away?

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:46.460
Yeah... Why did I?

00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:48.910
I wasn't able to be honest.

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:51.740
Well, if you know that, then it's all right, isn't it?

00:10:52.790 --> 00:10:56.810
All you have to do is be honest. Don't be so needlessly stubborn.

00:10:57.040 --> 00:10:57.680
But...

00:10:58.050 --> 00:10:59.580
"I'm sorry about before!"

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:02.590
That has to be the first thing you say to him.

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:07.070
Now then, everything from here on will cost, so how about it?

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:12.160
If she thinks about it too much, she'll self-destruct.

00:11:12.910 --> 00:11:14.530
Just like when she started school.

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:16.300
As always, huh?

00:11:17.250 --> 00:11:20.940
But if Katase can't function, then the mission can't be completed.

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:23.760
A chance. If she can just get a hold of one...

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:26.770
Please take care of it, Miss Instructor.

00:11:28.590 --> 00:11:29.540
I'll try and do it.

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:30.410
Sorry.

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:55.160
You kissed her all of a sudden?

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:55.800
Yes.

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:57.360
Before you told her how you felt?

00:11:57.760 --> 00:11:58.080
Yes.

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:02.850
That's incredible, I'm sure of it.

00:12:03.110 --> 00:12:06.030
At that time... it was natural to do it.

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:10.720
I didn't have any doubts, so it didn't bother me at all.

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:14.420
It would have been best to talk to her about it, right?

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:20.440
Why did I fall in love with her?

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:25.760
Good luck...

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:36.480
It's a strange feeling...

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:39.950
This is the most bustling place in the school, but...

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:43.830
All you have to do is think of it as summer vacation.

00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:47.130
When it's over, it'll go back to normal.

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:51.400
I wonder how it's going to turn out.

00:12:51.460 --> 00:12:55.190
I'm sure that it'll go well. They know how to deal with it.

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:58.700
Not the mission, but when we're found out.

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:00.770
Oh, I wonder.

00:13:01.290 --> 00:13:05.380
But it won't be counted as a crime. We're just staying behind.

00:13:05.570 --> 00:13:06.700
You're certainly easygoing.

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:08.090
R-Really?

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:11.880
I wonder when I'm going to get a girlfriend...

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:19.740
All right! It's a fake, but I'm finished packing my luggage!

00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:22.060
If we're found out, it'll affect our record, won't it?

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:23.760
It's more like we're definitely going to be found out.

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:27.100
It's not like we're going to be hiding the whole time.

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:28.860
I wonder if we're going to be expelled.

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:29.400
What?

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:31.570
Milady!

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:32.810
Kidding, I'm kidding!

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:33.830
Oh, you...

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:38.020
Although I don't know what we'll be able to do...

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:41.980
Well, that's fine, isn't it? Just wanting to be with her.

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:49.060
Have you finished your preparations to evacuate?

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:50.420
Yeah, a while ago!

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:51.580
I see.

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:56.090
Mom...

00:13:56.990 --> 00:14:00.110
I'm sorry. I've ruined our precious dinner, haven't I?

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:02.660
It's all right. It'll go well.

00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:03.260
Yes...

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:08.090
We're just parting for a little bit. Be sure to take care of yourself.

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:16.710
They even threw a flaming bottle at the Office of Space Development...

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:20.760
They think that only the government officials are going to evacuate.

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:24.050
Yet the whole world is confronting the crisis...

00:14:24.430 --> 00:14:26.710
It must seem completely unfair to them.

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:32.330
It certainly is foolish. But that man isn't the only one.

00:14:32.730 --> 00:14:37.600
The world is filled with anxiety. We just have to do our best.

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:38.170
Check.

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:40.100
No holding on.

00:14:40.710 --> 00:14:42.170
Tomorrow's the day, isn't it?

00:14:42.390 --> 00:14:42.940
Yes.

00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:47.590
I'm jealous. There's nothing as irritating as sitting and waiting.

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:49.720
That's what you get for becoming a politician.

00:14:51.210 --> 00:14:52.210
I'm counting on you.

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:54.500
I'm heading off.

00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:57.370
Just touching the Fracture, even a little...

00:14:57.660 --> 00:14:59.590
...and your atoms become disassembled, right?

00:14:59.770 --> 00:15:01.360
What, are you afraid?

00:15:01.850 --> 00:15:05.290
It'd be problematic, right? I wouldn't be able to see your cute face.

00:15:05.490 --> 00:15:06.590
So it's just my face.

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:08.530
No, that and this...

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:12.580
I'm going, so you're coming with me.

00:15:13.130 --> 00:15:15.210
Personally, I wanted to evacuate...

00:15:15.840 --> 00:15:16.510
Not allowed.

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:24.750
Hey.

00:15:25.180 --> 00:15:26.510
I'm sorry, calling you at a time like this.

00:15:27.010 --> 00:15:29.150
It's all right. What is it?

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:32.930
Well... we keep passing each other, right?

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:34.780
And...

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:38.110
I wanted to really talk to you.

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:41.930
Me, too...

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:45.370
There's something I want to talk about, too.

00:15:46.240 --> 00:15:46.700
What is it?

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:50.400
Until the mission is over, let's both just stay as pilots.

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:53.150
I think that would be good for now.

00:15:54.360 --> 00:15:56.240
You've already decided...

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:13.040
I'm sorry. All I've done is made you worry, all the way to the end.

00:16:13.710 --> 00:16:16.540
Really! And I told you to be honest, too!

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:19.170
But it was no good. I can't.

00:16:20.960 --> 00:16:23.480
That's why, right now, I have to focus on the mission.

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:26.780
All right! Let's watch TV or something!

00:16:27.270 --> 00:16:28.570
If I cry any more, my eyes will be swollen...

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:30.540
...and I won't be able to see what's in front of me!

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:38.230
May I? 

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:39.760
Hmm? What's wrong?

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:39.240
Yes. 

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:43.490
Shima-chan, hello!

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:46.360
This woman is the mother of Miss Shima Katase...

00:16:46.430 --> 00:16:49.940
...who was onboard the Infinity during the recent Great Mission.

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:51.010
What?!

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:57.980
At the end of last year, you went to space in a hurry...

00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:00.870
...and incidentally, when you were admitted to the Stellvia...

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:03.650
...you decided that in a hurry, too, and left.

00:17:04.340 --> 00:17:07.720
In the end, we've come this far without actually talking about it.

00:17:09.160 --> 00:17:14.810
No, that's half my fault. No, I know that it's mostly my fault.

00:17:15.650 --> 00:17:19.350
I knew you were thinking that you wanted to leave my house.

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:22.410
Of course, I knew. I'm your mother, after all.

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:29.040
But the selfish part of me is stronger than the understanding part.

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:32.450
I adore you! I love you!

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:35.510
Why couldn't I tell you when you were in front of me?

00:17:36.230 --> 00:17:38.350
I was embarrassed, so I wrote it in a letter...

00:17:38.690 --> 00:17:41.380
...but right now, if you're watching this on TV, then listen!

00:17:42.220 --> 00:17:43.090
Shima-chan...

00:17:43.980 --> 00:17:47.690
My daughter, I'm proud I gave birth to you...

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:50.920
Mother...

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:55.720
I met Umihito, we fell in love, loved each other...

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:58.900
...and then you were born.

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:01.040
That's why you're here.

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:05.340
Mother...

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:08.300
You are the pride and joy of both me and Umihito.

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:12.350
Do your best, Shima Katase! Do your best!

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:13.550
Do your best!

00:18:13.710 --> 00:18:14.690
Mother...

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:18.800
Our relaxed atmosphere has fallen apart, hasn't it?

00:18:21.340 --> 00:18:23.480
"That's why you're here," huh?

00:18:26.030 --> 00:18:26.930
W-What?

00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:35.280
I can't believe you tried to do so many things at once.

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:37.800
And to make matters worse, you don't have enough to say...

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:39.240
...so even if you covet her, it's useless, useless!

00:18:39.650 --> 00:18:41.210
I'm not coveting her or anything!

00:18:41.610 --> 00:18:43.670
In any case, right now, Shima-chan is right.

00:18:44.300 --> 00:18:46.270
For now, think only about the mission.

00:18:46.730 --> 00:18:50.250
Right now, it's impossible for you to deal with work and a romance.

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:52.110
What about you, big sister?

00:18:56.680 --> 00:18:57.580
Who was that just now?

00:18:58.130 --> 00:19:00.180
Do your best on the mission! Bye!

00:19:05.850 --> 00:19:07.570
A change to the Halcyon's specifications?

00:19:07.810 --> 00:19:10.560
Yes, sir. I want the DLS removed.

00:19:10.880 --> 00:19:12.870
I want to put the Bianca's system back in.

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:14.410
What do you think?

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:16.310
There's merit in testing it out.

00:19:16.600 --> 00:19:19.090
It means returning to an older system.

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:21.580
Just because something's new doesn't mean it's good.

00:19:22.330 --> 00:19:27.160
The DLS might be interfering with Katase's programming abilities.

00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:29.360
We'll try and confirm it in today's simulations.

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:32.730
I understand.

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:36.730
For now, let me look at the data. The answer will come after that.

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:37.600
Yes, sir.

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:42.310
There's no going back after this.

00:19:43.090 --> 00:19:45.690
That's fine... most likely.

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:55.380
Do your best.

00:19:56.690 --> 00:19:57.150
I will.

00:19:58.450 --> 00:19:59.490
Okay, we're going.

00:20:07.730 --> 00:20:09.060
Okay, as we planned.

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:09.960
Right...

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:25.580
The air is horrible...

00:20:26.690 --> 00:20:27.100
Shh!

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:29.590
Mice?

00:20:30.220 --> 00:20:33.780
It would be easier to live in the dust chute than in the air vents.

00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:42.950
I won't drag you down.

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:45.670
Let's both do our best.

00:20:48.040 --> 00:20:50.030
The Fujiyama's final flight just launched.

00:20:50.550 --> 00:20:51.620
The evacuation is finished.

00:20:52.170 --> 00:20:55.670
In one hour, the Stellvia will begin heading for Pluto.

00:20:56.940 --> 00:20:59.660
Hey, no one will spot us here, definitely.

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:01.860
You found a nice spot.

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:02.790
But...

00:21:03.740 --> 00:21:05.880
Wouldn't it have been better to hide in a tunnel?!

00:21:08.860 --> 00:21:13.490
Propulsion units one, two, three, four, five, and six are starting up.

00:21:14.180 --> 00:21:16.430
The Stellvia's internal gravity controls are all green.

00:21:16.980 --> 00:21:18.780
Generators are all go.

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:20.440
Propulsion units are all go.

00:21:20.950 --> 00:21:22.390
Systems are all go!

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:23.520
All right.

00:21:33.290 --> 00:21:34.950
Stellvia, move out!

